From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omer Faruk Nehir <omerfaruknehir@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 04:30:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] media: qcom: camss: quarantine direct AON MMIO

Both a read and a write to MAIN_CAM_AON_CAM_SEL_CTRL caused an abrupt platform
reset on the ASUS Zenbook A14. Runtime PM and both CPAS AHB clocks were proven
safe separately, so direct host MMIO access is not currently a valid handoff
mechanism on this platform.

Fail the provider API with -EOPNOTSUPP before touching the register. Keep the
resource discovery and ownership plumbing available for future replacement by
the correct firmware-mediated or platform-specific access path.

Signed-off-by: Omer Faruk Nehir <omerfaruknehir@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c | 25 ++++++-------------------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
index 000000000005..000000000006 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/camss/camss.c
@@ -73,6 +73,6 @@ int qcom_camss_aon_acquire(struct device *camss_dev)
 {
 	struct camss *camss;
+	int ret = -EOPNOTSUPP;
-	int ret;
 
 	if (!camss_dev)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -91,25 +92,8 @@ int qcom_camss_aon_acquire(struct device *camss_dev)
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
 
-	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(camss_dev);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		goto out_unlock;
-
-	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(X1E_CPAS_AON_CLK_COUNT,
-				      camss->aon_clks);
-	if (ret)
-		goto err_pm_put;
-
-	/* This register is write-only on the A14; reads reset the platform. */
-	writel(X1E_CPAS_AON_CAM_SEL_AON,
-	       camss->cpas_top_base + X1E_CPAS_AON_CAM_SEL_CTRL);
-
-	camss->aon_owned = true;
-	mutex_unlock(&camss->aon_lock);
-	return 0;
-
-err_pm_put:
-	pm_runtime_put(camss_dev);
+	dev_err_once(camss_dev,
+		     "AON handoff unavailable: direct CPAS MMIO resets this platform\n");
 out_unlock:
 	mutex_unlock(&camss->aon_lock);
 	return ret;
@@ -131,9 +118,8 @@ void qcom_camss_aon_release(struct device *camss_dev)
 	if (!camss->aon_owned)
 		goto out_unlock;
 
-	/* The AP state is known from the value written here; do not read back. */
-	writel(X1E_CPAS_AON_CAM_SEL_AP,
-	       camss->cpas_top_base + X1E_CPAS_AON_CAM_SEL_CTRL);
+	dev_warn_once(camss_dev,
+		      "dropping stale AON ownership without direct CPAS MMIO\n");
 
 	camss->aon_owned = false;
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(X1E_CPAS_AON_CLK_COUNT, camss->aon_clks);
-- 
